# Dagric OS — file search indexes NAMES, not the contents of every file.
#
# baloo6 ships enabled ("Setting up baloo6 (6.13.0-1)" in every build log) and
# its upstream default is to index file CONTENT: baloo_file_extractor opens
# every document, spreadsheet, PDF, ebook, archive and image in the home
# directory and pulls text out of it. Nothing in this tree configured it, so
# every Dagric machine has been doing that.
#
# On the hardware this OS is sold for, that lands at the worst possible moment.
# dagric-migrate rsyncs a Windows user's Documents, Desktop, Pictures, Music and
# Videos into $HOME — tens or hundreds of gigabytes — and the extractor then
# reads all of it back off a 5400 rpm platter, on two cores, while the owner is
# deciding what they think of the operating system.
#
# WHAT IS KEPT: "only basic indexing" still records every file's name, path,
# type and mtime, so the launcher and Dolphin still find files BY NAME — which
# is the only thing Dagric promises. manual/app-launcher.html says exactly that:
# "Find a document by name ... start typing the file name."
#
# WHAT IS GIVEN UP: searching INSIDE files. Nothing in the manual, the guide or
# the website offers it, and an owner who wants it ticks "Also index file
# content" in System Settings -> Search -> File Search, which rewrites this file.
#
# Indexing-Enabled is deliberately NOT set to false. Turning Baloo off outright
# would take filename search out of the launcher, and that IS a documented
# feature.

[General]
only basic indexing=true
